    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis three bedroom detached residence, located just off the scenic Westport to Leenane Road along the Wild Atlantic Way, is set on an elevated site offering distant views of Killary Fjord .\n\nBuilt circa 2005 the house was designed to maximize the countryside, mountain and water views to the front. The property has been very well maintained and comes to the market in excellent condition throughout.\n\nThe well proportioned floor area extends to approximately 144.5 sq m/1,555 sq ft. Accommodation comprises of a large entrance hall, living room, open plan kitchen/dining/sitting room, utility, three substantial bedrooms (master en-suite), bathroom, hotpress and coatpress. \n\nExternally, the property is set on a site of approximately 5.75 acres. \n\nThe gardens measure approximately 0.54 acre with lawns, south facing paved terrace, local stone walls and a gravel driveway with ample parking. There is a detached garage to the side with a roller door and electricity connection. \n\nThe additional 5.21 acres of land are located to the rear of the property. \n\nThe Leenane area is one of the most scenic locations in the West of Ireland. Leenane, a charming coastal village, is situated 3.3 km from the property. Its amenities include restaurants, cafes, shop and a hotel. It gained an international profile as the setting for the acclaimed film The Field. \n\nThe area is a haven for outdoor lovers with a choice of walking and hiking trails nearby including the Western Way. Glassilaun beach, a stunning white sand cove, is a ten minute drive and the famous Aasleagh Falls is less than 5 minutes away. The property is located between Clifden, 28 km distance, and Westport, 37 km distance. Ireland West International Airport is an hour and twenty minutes' drive.\n\nDirections: Coming from Westport take the Leenane Road, continue for 29.5km, take second left hand turn signposted Glennagevlagh after passing former Carraig Bar, the property is located on the right after 800 metres.\n\nOFFERS IN EXCESS OF 469,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.0m x 3.7m\nTiled floor, double doors to living room\n\nLiving Room - 6.4m x 4.3m\nCarpeted floor, cast iron open fireplace with wooden mantelpiece, feature apex window with views to Killary Fjord\n\nKitchen/Dining/Sitting Room - 6.2m x 4.2m & 4.0m x 4.0m\nTiled floor, maple shaker kitchen, oil fired range, free standing fridge, double doors to patio.\n\nUtility Room - 2.1m x 1.7m\nTiled floor, maple units, sink, access to garden\n\nBedroom One - 3.9m x 3.6m\nCarpeted floor, built in sliderobes, blinds\n\nBedroom Two - 3.4m x 3.0m\nCarpeted floor, built in sliderobes, blinds\n\nBedroom Three - 4.2m x 3.8m\nCarpeted floor, built in sliderobes, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 2.7m x 1.7m\nTiled floor and backsplash, electric shower, bath, wc, whb\n\nBathroom - 2.8m x 1.8m\nTiled floor and backsplash, bath, wc, whb\n\nStorage - 2.3m x 1.3m\nShelved\n\nCoatpress - \nShelved\n\n"
      },
      {
